From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Make generated documentation optional

License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (distribution build profile)
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

The generated website and PDF toolchain pulls hundreds of packages into a
clean build root. Add an explicit option that disables only generated
documentation while leaving the library, command-line tools, and complete
CTest suite unchanged. Packagers can install the man page sources shipped
in the release archive without running the website generators.

---
 CMakeLists.txt         |  6 +++++-
 etc/configure.cmake    |  2 ++
 srecord/CMakeLists.txt |  4 ++++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -39,0 +40,2 @@
+option(SRECORD_BUILD_DOCUMENTATION
+       "Build generated website, PDF, and API documentation" ON)
@@ -58 +60,3 @@
-add_subdirectory(doc)
+if(SRECORD_BUILD_DOCUMENTATION)
+  add_subdirectory(doc)
+endif()
--- a/etc/configure.cmake
+++ b/etc/configure.cmake
@@ -106,0 +107 @@
+if(SRECORD_BUILD_DOCUMENTATION)
@@ -134,0 +136 @@
+endif()
--- a/srecord/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/srecord/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -36,0 +37 @@
+if(SRECORD_BUILD_DOCUMENTATION)
@@ -39,0 +41 @@
+endif()
@@ -46,0 +48 @@
+if(SRECORD_BUILD_DOCUMENTATION)
@@ -49,0 +52 @@
+endif()
